Here is the full **testsmells.org 19-smell academic audit** of `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`.

---

## Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High | 2 | 2 |
| Medium | 2 | 2 |
| Low | 0 | 0 |
| **Total** | **4** | **4** |

> **Integration-test calibration applied.** The class is marked `[TestCategory("Integration")]`, so Mystery Guest, Eager Test, and Sleepy Test severities are downgraded per the academic calibration rules. 4 of the 8 tests are clean.

---

## Findings by Severity

### 🔴 HIGH — Conditional Test Logic

**Smell:** Conditional Test Logic (testsmells.org core smell #1)
**Test:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` — line 101
**Why it matters:** The `if`/`else` means only one assertion branch runs per execution. If `loaded` is always a base `User`, the `PremiumUser` path is dead code giving false coverage. If it's always a `PremiumUser`, the `Name` check never runs.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — one branch is always dead
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Fix:** Split into two explicit tests with deterministic setup:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_StandardUser_ReturnsCorrectName()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");
    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_PremiumUser_HasPositiveDiscount()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("eve@example.com", "Eve", discountRate: 0.1m));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com") as PremiumUser;
    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Hidden testing gap — one code path is never verified.

---

### 🔴 HIGH — Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test)

**Smell:** Unknown Test / Empty Test (testsmells.org core smell #4)
**Test:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` — lines 113–119
**Why it matters:** This test inserts 100 rows but asserts nothing. It passes as long as no exception is thrown, even if every insert silently fails or corrupts data. The name "RunsWithoutErrors" suggests a "does not throw" intent, but that should be made explicit.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — zero assertions
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
}
```

**Fix:** Add verification of the outcome:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False confidence — 100% pass rate with 0% verified behavior.

---

### 🟡 MEDIUM — Sleepy Test *(downgraded from High — integration calibration)*

**Smell:** Sleepy Test (testsmells.org core smell #3)
**Test:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` — line 87
**Why it matters:** `Thread.Sleep(3000)` adds 3 seconds of wall-clock time per run. If the notification is faster, you waste time; if it's slower, you get a flaky failure. Research (Camara et al., SAST 2021) correlates sleep-based waits with flaky test rates.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — hard-coded 3-second sleep
Thread.Sleep(3000);
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

**Fix:** Poll with a timeout instead:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var timeout = TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5);
    var interval = TimeSpan.FromMilliseconds(100);
    var sw = Stopwatch.StartNew();

    while (sw.Elapsed < timeout)
    {
        if (_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id))
            break;
        await Task.Delay(interval);
    }

    Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id),
        "Notification was not sent within the timeout period.");
}
```

> *Note:* Severity downgraded from High → Medium because the class is tagged `[TestCategory("Integration")]` and async coordination waits are more common in integration contexts. It is still a smell because polling or event-based waits are strictly superior.

**Risk if unfixed:** 3 s of waste per run; flaky failures if the system is slower than 3 s.

---

### 🟡 MEDIUM — Assertion Roulette

**Smell:** Assertion Roulette (testsmells.org extended smell)
**Test:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` — lines 35–38
**Why it matters:** Four assertions with no message parameters. When one fails, the MSTest output shows a line number but no explanation — you must read the code to understand *which property* was wrong and *why*.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — 4 assertions, zero messages
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

**Fix:** Add explanatory messages:

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert.");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should be persisted.");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should be persisted.");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Auto-generated Id should be positive.");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Slower failure diagnosis in CI logs.

---

## Smells Scanned and NOT Found (Clean)

The following 15 smells from the full testsmells.org taxonomy were checked and **no instances detected** — this is a positive signal:

| Smell | Status | Notes |
|-------|--------|-------|
| Mystery Guest | ✅ Clean | SQLite in-memory is hermetic; integration-calibrated |
| Eager Test | ✅ Clean | No test calls 4+ distinct production methods |
| Magic Number Test | ✅ Clean | `3` and `10` in count assertions are self-documenting (items just added) |
| Sensitive Equality | ✅ Clean | No `.ToString()` comparisons |
| Exception Handling | ✅ Clean | No `try`/`catch` blocks in tests |
| General Fixture | ✅ Clean | `_connection` and `_repository` are used by all 8 tests |
| Ignored/Disabled Test | ✅ Clean | No `[Ignore]` or skip attributes |
| Duplicate Assert | ✅ Clean | No repeated identical assertions |
| Lazy Test | ✅ Clean | Tests sharing `Insert`/`GetByEmail` test distinct behaviors |
| Constructor Initialization | ✅ Clean | Properly uses `[TestInitialize]` |
| Default Test | ✅ Clean | Class name is meaningful |
| Redundant Print | ✅ Clean | No `Console.WriteLine` calls |
| Redundant Assertion | ✅ Clean | No tautological assertions |
| Resource Optimism | ✅ Clean | In-memory DB created fresh per test |
| Empty Test | ✅ Clean | No completely empty test bodies |

## Well-Written Tests

`DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase`, `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted`, `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord`, and `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` are well-structured: clear arrange-act-assert, focused scope, meaningful assertions, and no smells.

---

## Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Test | Effort | Action |
|----------|-------|------|--------|--------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` | 🟢 Low | Add a count assertion — 1 line |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` | 🟡 Med | Split into 2 deterministic tests |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` | 🟡 Med | Replace `Thread.Sleep` with poll loop |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette | `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` | 🟢 Low | Add message strings to each `Assert` |

Fixes 1 and 4 are quick wins (minutes). Fixes 2 and 3 require slightly more thought but eliminate the two most dangerous patterns: hidden dead code and non-deterministic timing.
